{"value": {"url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-seata/pulls/7815", "id": 3052962431, "node_id": "PR_kwDOCb0Xyc61-IJ_", "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/incubator-seata/pull/7815", "diff_url": "https://github.com/apache/incubator-seata/pull/7815.diff", "patch_url": "https://github.com/apache/incubator-seata/pull/7815.patch", "issue_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-seata/issues/7815", "commits_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-seata/pulls/7815/commits", "review_comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-seata/pulls/7815/comments", "review_comment_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-seata/pulls/comments{/number}", "comments_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-seata/issues/7815/comments", "statuses_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-seata/statuses/42b13d0a303e51b606a34c82891a81a8affb7564", "number": 7815, "state": "closed", "locked": false, "title": "test: fix combine test to avoid failure due to ordering", "user": {"login": "cperkkk", "id": 52606428, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjUyNjA2NDI4", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/52606428?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/cperkkk", "html_url": "https://github.com/cperkkk", "followers_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cperkkk/followers", "following_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cperkkk/following{/other_user}", "gists_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cperkkk/gists{/gist_id}", "starred_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cperkkk/starred{/owner}{/repo}", "subscriptions_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cperkkk/subscriptions", "organizations_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cperkkk/orgs", "repos_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cperkkk/repos", "events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cperkkk/events{/privacy}", "received_events_url": "https://api.github.com/users/cperkkk/received_events", "type": "User", "user_view_type": "public", "site_admin": false}, "body": "<!--\r\n    Licensed to the Apache Software Foundation (ASF) under one or more\r\n    contributor license agreements.  See the NOTICE file distributed with\r\n    this work for additional information regarding copyright ownership.\r\n    The ASF licenses this file to You under the Apache License, Version 2.0\r\n    (the \"License\"); you may not use this file except in compliance with\r\n    the License.  You may obtain a copy of the License at\r\n\r\n    http://www.apache.org/licenses/LICENSE-2.0\r\n    \r\n    Unless required by applicable law or agreed to in writing, software\r\n    distributed under the License is distributed on an \"AS IS\" BASIS,\r\n    WITHOUT WARRANTIES OR CONDITIONS OF ANY KIND, either express or implied.\r\n    See the License for the specific language governing permissions and\r\n    limitations under the License.\r\n-->\r\n<!-- Please make sure you have read and understood the contributing guidelines -->\r\n\r\n- [x] I have read the [CONTRIBUTING.md](https://github.com/apache/incubator-seata/blob/2.x/CONTRIBUTING.md) guidelines.\r\n- [x] I have registered the PR [changes](https://github.com/apache/incubator-seata/tree/2.x/changes).\r\n\r\n### \u2160. Describe what this PR did\r\nThis pull request addresses several flaky test, in the\u00a0`apache/incubator-seata`\u00a0project. The test was failing \r\nintermittently due to assumptions about the ordering of the test. I've noticed that when running the test in specific ordering will produce a test failure (maven surefire plugin unfortunately does not guarantee test ordering), such as:\r\n\r\n```\r\nmvn test -Dtest=org.apache.seata.config.AbstractConfigurationTest#AtestGetConfigWithNull+BtestGetConfigWithDefaultValue\r\n```\r\n\r\nThe tests will fail with output:\r\n\r\n```\r\nERROR] Failures:\r\n[ERROR]   AbstractConfigurationTest.AtestGetConfigWithNull:152 expected: not <null>\r\n```\r\n\r\nThis is due to the necessity of the cache being set by `testGetConfigWithDefaultValue` first, before the eventual `testGetConfigWithNull` running for it to pass. So there's an assumed ordering but the test fails to explicitly guarantee the ordering (different version of maven surefire will run the order randomly and if the test are refactored / renamed, the current test order will change and it will fail), combining the test will help with removing this flakiness.\r\n\r\n### \u2161. Does this pull request fix one issue?\r\nIt does not fixes a particular github issue.\r\n\r\n\r\n### \u2162. Why don't you add test cases (unit test/integration test)? \r\nI've only changed test and not code under test\r\n\r\n### \u2163. Describe how to verify it\r\nWe test the combined version\r\n\r\n```\r\nmvn test -Dtest=org.apache.seata.config.AbstractConfigurationTest#testGetConfigWithDefaultValue\r\n```\r\n\r\n```\r\n[INFO] ------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n[INFO] BUILD SUCCESS\r\n[INFO] ------------------------------------------------------------------------\r\n```\r\n\r\n### \u2164. Special notes for reviews\r\n- The fix ensures the test is robust to non-deterministic behaviors of ordering, making it compatible with future updates  to it or related dependencies.\r\n\r\nLet me know if further improvements or clarifications are needed!\r\n", "labels": [], "milestone": {"id": 13232761, "node_id": "MI_kwDOCb0Xyc4Ayep5", "url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-seata/milestones/40", "html_url": "https://github.com/apache/incubator-seata/milestone/40", "labels_url": "https://api.github.com/repos/apache/incubator-seata/milestones/40/labels", "number": 40, "state": "closed", "title": "2.6.0", "description": "", "creator": {"login": "slievrly", "id": 8758457, "node_id": "MDQ6VXNlcjg3NTg0NTc=", "avatar_url": "https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/8758457?v=4", "gravatar_id": "", "url": "https://api.github.com/users/slievrly", "html_url": "https://github.com/slievrly", "followers_url": "https://api.github.